'''Hornindalsvatnet'''<ref name="KV">{{Cite web |title=Informasjon om stadnamn |url=https://stadnamn.kartverket.no/fakta/192617 |access-date=2025-05-10 |website=Norgeskart |publisher=[[Norwegian Mapping Authority|Kartverket]] |language=no}}</ref> is [[Norway]]'s and [[Europe]]'s [[Lakes in Norway#Deepest lakes|deepest lake]],<ref name="snl">{{Cite SNL|Hornindalsvatnet|Hornindalsvatnet|2025-05-10|Haugen|Morten O.|2024-11-26}}</ref> and the world's fourteenth [[List of lakes by depth|deepest lake]], officially measured to a depth of {{convert|514|m|ft|abbr=on}}. Its surface lies {{convert|53|m|ft|abbr =on}} above [[sea level]], which means that its bottom is {{convert|461|m|ft|abbr=on}} below sea level.

The village of [[Grodås]] lies at the eastern end of the lake in [[Volda Municipality]] in [[Møre og Romsdal]] county and the village of [[Mogrenda]] is located on the western end of the lake in [[Stad Municipality]] in [[Vestland]] county. The [[European route E39]] highway runs near the lake. The village of [[Heggjabygda]] and [[Heggjabygda Church]] lie on the northern shore of the lake.

Its volume is estimated at {{convert|12|km3|cumi|abbr=on}}, its area is {{convert|51|km2|sqmi|abbr=on}} and ranks 19th in area among Norway's lakes. The main outflow is the river Eidselva, which flows into the Eidsfjorden, an arm off the main [[Nordfjorden (Vestland)|Nordfjorden]].<ref name="snl" />

The deepest point of the lake was explored using a [[Remotely operated underwater vehicle|ROV]] in 2006.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Søreide |first=Fredrik |title=Secrets of Europe's deepest lakes. Discoveries from Norway |journal=Sea Technology |volume=55 |issue=5 |pages=39–42}}</ref> A small white fish was discovered on the lake bottom – probably a new species of [[Arctic char|Arctic charr]] (''Salvelinus alpinus''). It was previously also located in [[Tinnsjå|Lake Tinn]], Norway's third deepest lake.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Søreide |first=Fredrik |title=Den mystiske dypvannsfisken i Tinnsjøen |journal=Fauna |volume=59 |issue=4 |pages=122–129}}</ref>

The lake is the site of the Hornindalsvatnet [[Marathon]], held annually in July.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Hornindalsvatnet Maraton |url=http://home.online.no/~iahaugen/maraton/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100818123918/http://home.online.no/~iahaugen/maraton/ |archive-date=2010-08-18 |access-date=2010-07-11 |language=no}}</ref>

